Relevant columns and their potential usage
• GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_BOUNDARIES.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_WAYS  
  – "id": unique identifier of each way – needed to distinguish two different roads.  
  – "geometry": GEOMETRY line‑string/multi‑line string of the road – used with ST_INTERSECTS to detect overlap.  
  – "all_tags": VARIANT array that stores every OSM tag – filter for `"highway"` classes (motorway, trunk, primary, secondary, residential) and be sure the key `"bridge"` is absent.  
  – "nodes": VARIANT array with the ordered list of node‑ids that compose the way – two different ways must NOT share any common node.  

• GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_BOUNDARIES.GEO_US_BOUNDARIES.STATES  
  – "state": 2–letter state code (e.g. CA).  
  – "state_geom": GEOMETRY polygon – lets us keep only the ways that lie (intersect) in California.  

Conditions that will ultimately be needed  
1. Highway class filter  
   EXISTS (SELECT 1  
           FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => w."all_tags") t  
           WHERE t.value:"key"::STRING = 'highway'  
             AND t.value:"value"::STRING IN ('motorway','trunk','primary','secondary','residential'))  

2. Exclude bridge objects  
   NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1  
               FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => w."all_tags") t  
               WHERE t.value:"key"::STRING = 'bridge')  

3. Located in California  
   ST_INTERSECTS(w."geometry", ca."state_geom") = TRUE  

4. Two different ways overlap but do NOT share nodes  
   ST_INTERSECTS(w1."geometry", w2."geometry") = TRUE  
   NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1  
               FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => w1."nodes") n1  
               JOIN LATERAL FLATTEN(input => w2."nodes") n2  
                 ON n1.value = n2.value)  

